.page mkdir 1 make directories

# SYNOPSIS
*mkdir* [*-p*] [*-m* _MODE_] _DIRECTORY_...

# DESCRIPTION
`mkdir` creates each _DIRECTORY_. It is an error if the directory exists or if its parent does not, unless `-p` is given.

# OPTIONS
@ *-p*
    Create missing parent directories as needed. A directory that already exists is not an error.
@ *-m* _MODE_
    Give the new directories the permissions _MODE_, an octal number. The default is 755.

# EXIT STATUS
0, 1 if a directory could not be created, 2 for an unknown option.

# EXAMPLES
    mkdir projects
    mkdir -p /tmp/a/b/c
    mkdir -m 700 private

# SEE ALSO
rmdir(1), rm(1), chmod(1)
